node_modules/
.svelte-kit/

# `build/` USED TO BE HERE AND IS DELIBERATELY NOT.
#
# It is generated output, and generated output is normally not committed. This
# one is, for a reason that is not about tidiness: the Rust binary serves it,
# and the operator's requirement is `git clone`, open the project, press Run —
# with no package manager on the machine and no second process. An ignored
# `build/` means a fresh clone has nothing to serve, and the only way back is a
# command, which is the thing being removed.
#
# D-0053 already licenses this in as many words: "If a build step is
# introduced, its OUTPUT is committed under `web/`, so a clone with no Node
# still builds a working binary." D-0064 is the entry that takes it up.
#
# `crates/api` still does not depend on this directory to BUILD — it is read at
# run time and its absence is a page that says so. See `crates/api/src/assets.rs`.

# The dev server's dependency cache. Build output, and it reappears whenever
# `vite dev` runs.
.vite/
